      "section": "opening",
      "slot": "opening",
      "text": "Aspose.Cells FOSS for Python reads and writes Excel .xlsx workbooks, converts them to .csv, .tsv, .json, .markdown, .md, .pdf, and .xlsm formats, and supports encryption and decryption of .xlsx files. It reads .xlsx workbooks and loads .csv data using load_csv_workbook and CSVLoadOptions. It provides classes such as Workbook, Worksheet, Cells, Cell, Style, and DataValidation to create, modify, and style workbooks, apply data validation rules, and manage charts, pictures, shapes, tables, and sparklines."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:001",
        "example:002",
        "format:input.xlsx",
        "format:output.xlsx",
        "public_symbol:aspose.cells_foss.cell",
        "public_symbol:aspose.cells_foss.cells",
        "public_symbol:aspose.cells_foss.workbook",
        "public_symbol:aspose.cells_foss.worksheet"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:1",
      "text": "It reads and writes Excel workbooks in .xlsx format, allowing users to create new workbooks, access worksheets via the Workbook.worksheets collection, and read or write cell values using A1-style references through the Cells and Cell objects."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:003",
        "public_symbol:aspose.cells_foss.cell",
        "public_symbol:aspose.cells_foss.font",
        "public_symbol:aspose.cells_foss.style"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:2",
      "text": "It applies fonts, fills, borders, alignment, and number formats to cells using the Style, Font, and related objects, enabling bold text, custom colors, and size adjustments that persist when saving workbooks."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:004",
        "public_symbol:aspose.cells_foss.datavalidation",
        "public_symbol:aspose.cells_foss.datavalidationalertstyle",
